WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had your kids on set.
-Yeah.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
-7, 10...13?

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Here´s a photo of your kids.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-They´re very adorable.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I haven´t even
seen that picture.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.077
-And they were on set with you.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were on set with me...
-I think for that clip.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...for the clip
that you guys just saw,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.983
which is the introduction
of my father, John Lithgow.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we are --
we´re very open, loving...

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.887
-Mm-hmm.
-...father and son relationship.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
We kiss every time
we greet each other.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was the scene they
got to see for the first time.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.863
Which I -- I forgot that we were
shooting it that day,

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my boys were like,
"What is going on?"

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.237
I was like, "Well, is it funny?"

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It´s funny,
but it´s embarrassing."

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How many more times
do you guys gotta kiss?"

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m like,
"We´ll do it all day long."

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What?!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We will do it all day long."
Yeah, so, uh...

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.052 size:81% position:41%
They thought it was --
-They learned that --

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.521
-They were like,
"Dad, your job´s embarrassing."

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know one of your kids
recently asked you --

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s obviously smart
to know that this is a thing.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He wanted a gap year.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wanted to take a gap year.
-Yes.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s in 8th grade.
-Okay.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-And, uh...

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said,
"Hey, dad, I think, uh...

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I want to do
a gap year."

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go,
"Between 8th and 9th grade?

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like when?
Right now?"

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s like, "No, no, college.
I want to do a gap year."

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m like,
"Oh, well, you know,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.148
I think that that´s something a
lot of kids are talking about."

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
´Cause, you know,
it´s hard to really know

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you´re 17, 18...
-Sure.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:28.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...what you want to do, and,
"Yeah, if you want

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:31.024
to go get a job or work for
the, you know, Peace Corps

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:34.094
or do something like that,"
and he´s like, "Work? No.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:37.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s called a gap year, Dad."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.098 size:75% position:38%
"You just hang out."

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like,
"You do not just hang out."

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You have to do something
constructive."

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.205
He´s like, "You don´t know
what you´re talking about."

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"It´s a gap year."

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that will be
an ongoing argument, I think,

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.412 size:84% position:42%
in our household, yeah.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.347
-Well, I hope -- You know, I
don´t know who I´m rooting for,

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I hope you guys
figure it out.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.751
I want to talk to you about
this, because we´ve done

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very popular segment
on our show,

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.188
called "Second Chance Theater."
-Yes, which I love, yes.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So we´ve done it --
I think we´ve had 605 shows.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we´ve done it
three times.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-So it was very popular.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
There´s a sketch of yours

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I remember
right when I started "SNL"...

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...it was like a thing

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we would
all gather around and watch.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.903
-As one of the biggest failing
sketches at dress of all time.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I, uh --
And it is --

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you explain it,
it will sound like something

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
that should fail,
don´t you think?

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There´s no question.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It´s based on --

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s based on --

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wrote a sketch
about a guy who dresses --

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.186
looks exactly like Gabe Kaplan,

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:36.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was the star of the hit
sitcom "Welcome Back, Kotter."

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.758
-"Welcome Back, Kotter," yeah.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was also
a professional gambler.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-Side note.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wrote a sketch
where it was --

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
I worked
for an insurance company...

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.970
And it took place in a
break room, and everyone was --

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.406
It´s the day
that Gabe Kaplan came to visit.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.908 size:81% position:41%
-The real Gabe Kaplan.
-The real Gabe Kaplan,

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.911
and no one came to get me
out of the bathroom to meet him

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause I was his biggest fan.
-Yeah, right.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.650
-And judging by the silence
in this room, you can tell...

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
...that it didn´t work then,
and it will never work.

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that´s why
we need to bring it back...

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.823
-We have to bring it back.
-...for "Second Chance Theater."

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, here´s the thing
about it.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.895
´Cause the interesting thing is,
you realize the core

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:19.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
problem with this sketch
is that no one --

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
there´s a lack of recognition
for Gabe Kaplan...

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.702 size:84% position:42%
-Sure, for Gabe Kaplan.
-...right off the jump.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Super...
-And now it´s been 17 years.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:26.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Super obscure
late ´70s reference.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And so now time has passed.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would argue that,
if anything, he´s less known.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Less relevant.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.981
-But you´d be willing to come
and do the Gabe Kaplan sketch.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I would in a heartbeat.
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.552 size:84% position:42%
-And I´d say the reason
it was great to watch

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:43.256
and why we all watched it,
is you never waned at all.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right.
-You committed fully.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I have a tendency,
for some reason,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I could tell --
when a sketch was tanking,

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I could tell
the audience was like,

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Let´s just get
to the next thing,

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
" I would take twice as long.
-Yeah.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t know why,

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:02.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I wanted
to punish the audience.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like, "Okay.
You don´t think it´s funny.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.113 size:84% position:42%
Now you´re gonna really
not think it´s funny."

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.650 size:81% position:41%
"´Cause I´m gonna turn
this three-minute gem

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
into a eight-minute turd.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you´re gonna have
to sit through it.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And most of the dialogue...
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.758
-...is you saying to Horatio,
John Goodman, I believe...

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.793 size:84% position:42%
-John Goodman and Molly
and Tim Meadows, maybe.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:24.163
...is just a lot --
You just keep repeating, "What?"

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.767
-"What?
Why wouldn´t you come get me?!"

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
"My life
is all about Gabe Kaplan."

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.607 size:84% position:42%
So, yeah, I really --
-Next time you´re here,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.142 size:78% position:39%
we´re gonna break out
the Kaplan mask...

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Done. Beautiful.
-...and go to work.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

